# Deliberately NOT denylisted, though they look machine-bound:
#   builtInPluginSettings  -- two keyboard triggers; tooling/dms/validate-overlay
#                             has a dedicated validator for its shape.
#   customThemeFile        -- templated with ${HOME} and the theme itself ships
#                             as a create_ seed, so it is portable by construction.

# Moved out of SettingsSpec at DMS config v15, so they can no longer reach
# settings.json and no longer belong on a list whose contract is "one exact
# top-level SettingsSpec key per line". SettingsStore.js names them in
# SESSION_MOVED_KEYS (niriOutputSettings, hyprlandOutputSettings,
# activeDisplayProfile, activeDisplayProfileModes, desktopWidgetGridSettings,
# greeterSyncPending, greeterSyncBaseline, lastAppliedIconTheme -> session.json)
# and CACHE_MOVED_KEYS (browserUsageHistory, filePickerUsageHistory ->
# cache.json). Nothing is unguarded by their removal: tooling/dms/capture only
# offers a key tooling/dms/defaults reports, and tooling/dms/validate-overlay
# rejects any overlay key absent from that same schema, so a key outside
# SettingsSpec is unreachable by both paths. tooling/validate/all asserts every
# line here still exists in the schema, which is what surfaced them.
